WEBVTT

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:11.005
Investment Funds
Capture a fund subscription and follow it to the transfer agent, with the controls the regulator expects.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:17.560
Sign in as Vanessa Ah-Kee — Fund Manager
Fund Manager — captures and follows client fund orders

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:24.640
Funds: the Genesis Global Funds range
Asset class, horizon, AUM held by our clients and number of share classes

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:32.280
Share classes: what the client actually buys
Currency, risk rating 1–5, minimum investment and the latest NAV

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:39.760
Each share class holds the dealing rules
ISIN, entry and exit fees, dealing frequency and the cut-off time

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:47.600
NAV History: one price per share class per dealing date
Synced from the transfer agent — holdings are valued at the latest NAV

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.880
Fund Orders ▸ Fund subscription opens a three-step wizard
Investor & fund → amount & payment → suitability

00:00:52.880 --> 00:01:02.600
First, a client whose KYC is still in progress
Amit Lebrasse — let's see what the system does

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:12.600
The amount is in the share class currency — here US dollars
Minimum subscription USD 50,000 for the FMB 2029

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:19.200
Payment not received yet, so "Payment proof received" stays unticked
We come back to it before the checks

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:26.040
Refused: orders are accepted only for clients with approved KYC
The rule is checked on the server — no one can skip it

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:36.440
Switch to Natacha Hardy — KYC approved, conservative profile
Her risk profile allows products up to risk 1; the FMB 2029 is rated 2

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:46.160
Refused again: the fund is riskier than her profile
Record why the client still wants it, and that she acknowledged the higher risk

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.120
With the override documented, capture the order
The fund manager is recorded as the maker

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:54.880
Order captured — an operations checker will authorise it
It starts in the Captured stage

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:02.640
On the pipeline, move the order to Checks complete
This is the hand-off to Operations

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.200
Blocked: the payment proof must be received first
A stage gate — the order cannot reach Operations without it

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:15.360
The client's transfer has arrived — tick "Payment proof received"
Edit the order

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:20.080
Move it again
Now the gate lets it through and an approval is raised

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:26.080
An approval request goes to the operations checkers
Maker-checker: the person who captured the order can never approve it

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.360
Vanessa has nothing to approve here
Her own order is routed to Operations, not to her

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.960
The operations checker reviews and approves
Tools ▸ Approvals

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:38.800
Sign in as Ritesh Seewoo — Operations Checker
Operations Checker — authorises fund orders

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:56.480
He opens the order first: payment proof, amount, suitability override
The checker sees everything the maker recorded — but cannot change it

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:05.960
Approved — the system does the rest
Sends the order to the transfer agent, records its reference, confirms, emails the client and books the units

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:09.560
Back with the fund manager: the order is Confirmed
Sent to TA → Confirmed, without anyone typing it in

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:15.360
Sign in as Vanessa Ah-Kee — Fund Manager
Fund Manager — checks the outcome

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:22.360
The transfer agent's reference is on the order: TA-6175483
Units allotted are worked out at the latest NAV

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:27.800
The client was emailed a confirmation
In her own language — logged on the order's activity

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:31.280
The audit trail: who captured, who approved, every stage change
Maker and checker are always two different people

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:44.840
Fund Holdings: her new FMB 2029 units
Units × latest NAV = value, with the gain against book cost

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:50.840
Fund Campaigns: the FMB 2029 series
Planned → Window open → Allocating → Closed

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:55.360
Series 2 is open: target, amount subscribed and progress
Every subscription linked to the campaign counts, converted to rupees

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:09.720
The Investment Funds dashboard
Holdings value, investors, orders awaiting the TA and the campaign raise

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:16.278
Subscriptions vs redemptions, orders by fund and per month
Each widget opens the records behind it

00:04:16.278 --> 00:04:26.760
A fund subscription, end to end
